<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 275 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 275 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 275 million stg of unspecified late assistance.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.1 BLN    1.1 BLN    1.15 BLN   1.15 BLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    550 MLN    784 MLN    834 MLN    1.109 BLN</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   250 MLN*   64 MLN*    =	    =</p>
<p> BAND 1  T BILLS		     32 MLN*</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS		  138 MLN*     50 MLN*</p>
<p> BILLS/FRG TO DEC 9   300 MLN#   =	    =	    =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED ASSISTANCE					  275 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p># INTEREST RATE - 5-31/32 PCT</p>
</text>
